      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This is a very common phenomenon known as \"phantom wake words,\" which is actually a known software glitch where the microphone picks up background noise like a car alarm or a phone ringing and falsely triggers the device. The smart locks clicking and lights dimming are simply the automated routines responding to those false wake-up signals, creating a spooky but harmless chain reaction. You are not being paranoid; your system is just experiencing a temporary glitch that can be fixed by updating the firmware or adjusting the wake-word sensitivity settings.",
      "source": "target",
